(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "ADR-2608196900")
  (:adr/title "the floor's premise was falsified three days after it was written: 16 appviews migrated off Svelte")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-08-19")
  (:adr/tags "detectors evidence-floor calibration co-scientist")
  (:adr/body
  "## The question left open yesterday

ADR-2608196800 fixed the tick so a refusal is no longer recorded as a clean sweep,
and deliberately did **not** touch the floor that was causing the refusal:

    Do not lower the floor to make the check answerable -- that is the instinct
    this floor exists to defeat. The question to answer first is why the input
    shrank.

This is that answer.

## Why the input shrank

Comparing the repositories named in the baseline finding set against the
repositories carrying a candidate page today: **16 in the baseline have no page
now.** They are not missing checkouts. `cloud-itonami/aidesk` `c44f316`, dated
today:

    refactor: migrate the appview from TypeScript/Svelte to ClojureScript

    wrangler.jsonc's main pointed at svelte/.svelte-kit/cloudflare/_worker.js --
    a SvelteKit build output absent from the tree -- while the file that read
    like the application ... was referenced by no code at all

`svelte/src/routes/+page.svelte` no longer exists in those repositories, so they
stopped being candidates. Candidates fell from ~164 to 142, under the floor of 150,
and the detector refused.

## The sentence that was wrong

The floor carried its own justification, written 2026-08-16:

    Candidates only fall when the input is actually missing, which is the thing
    worth refusing on.

Three days. The paragraph directly above it anticipates *deleting the dead summary
object* as a legitimate repair that must not trigger a refusal -- and then misses
the same repair one level up: **deleting the page that carried it.**

## Change

The floor is now sized against the threat it names -- an un-populated `orgs/`, a
wrong `--root`, a tree that never got checked out -- and not against attrition of
Svelte appviews, which is a population that should be free to fall to zero.
**150 -> 50**: well below anything ever measured (225 pages on 2026-08-16, 142
candidates today) and far above what a mis-rooted run finds, which is none.

A line is also printed for the count that actually moved:

    svelte-dirs-without-a-page=68 (migrated away, or never had one -- NOT missing input)

so the next reader can tell a migration from a missing checkout without repeating
the archaeology this took.

## Both directions

    the real tree        exit 1, 296 findings   (it was refusing entirely -- these were invisible)
    --root <empty dir>   exit 2, CANNOT ANSWER: no +page.svelte under .../orgs

296 rather than the baseline's 337 is the 16 migrated repositories, correctly gone.

## What this pair of ADRs says together

Yesterday: a refusal that the registry could not hear. Today: a refusal that was
correct machinery reacting to a stale premise. **Both were right locally and wrong
in composition** -- and the second one had its premise written down in the file, in
prose, next to the constant, which is the best case for catching it and still took
a day and an outside question.

A floor is a claim about the world. It should say what it is defending against, and
be sized against that -- not against the population that happened to exist the
afternoon it was written.")))
